2026-10-18 08:02:13 | task=fp-filter | iter=22 | call=record_verdict({"finding": "[connection notification and tasklet scheduling] net/smc/smc_loopback.c:164\n\nRace on conn->killed check without lock protection. At line 164, `if (conn && !conn->killed)` checks the connection's killed flag without holding smcd->lock. The killed flag is set in smc_conn_kill() (net/smc/smc_core.c:1443) and the connection can be freed independently. Even if conn is non-NULL at line 164, it could be freed before line 165 `tasklet_schedule(&conn->rx_tsklet)`. The regular ISM implementation (smcd_handle_irq in smc_ism.c:526-528) holds smcd->lock during the entire conn read and tasklet schedule, preventing this race. The loopback path should similarly hold smcd->lock when accessing conn and scheduling its tasklet.", "impact": "high", "verdict": "keep", "reason": "Real race condition: conn->killed is read and tasklet is scheduled without holding smcd->lock, while smc_ism_unset_conn and smc_conn_kill can free the connection. The conn pointer read without smcd->lock could be stale or point to freed memory.", "proof": ""}) | ok=True
2026-10-18 08:02:21 | task=fp-filter | iter=23 | call=record_verdict({"finding": "[index bounds and connection array mapping] net/smc/smc_loopback.c:163\n\nsba_idx used to index smcd->conn without bounds validation at access time. While smc_lo_register_dmb validates sba_idx < SMC_LO_MAX_DMBS (5000) during allocation, smc_lo_move_data uses rmb_node->sba_idx (originally set during registration) to index smcd->conn[] without re-validating. If a DMB node was registered before SMC_LO_MAX_DMBS was changed, or if the token lookup finds a stale/corrupted node, the index could be out of bounds. Additionally, the conn array is sized to max_dmbs (SMC_LO_MAX_DMBS) in smcd_lo_alloc_dev, but there's no runtime check that rmb_node->sba_idx < ARRAY_SIZE(smcd->conn). The regular ISM path relies on the hardware IRQ handler providing a valid dmbno from the device itself, whereas the loopback path trusts a stored index from a user-controlled registration.", "impact": "medium", "verdict": "drop", "reason": "False positive: sba_idx is validated during registration (for_each_clear_bit iterates 0..SMC_LO_MAX_DMBS-1), the hash lookup is protected by dmb_ht_lock preventing stale reads, and smcd->conn is allocated with the same SMC_LO_MAX_DMBS size. The token-based lookup prevents finding a \"stale/corrupted\" node since the lock protects the hash table.", "proof": "In smc_lo_register_dmb (lines 60-64): for_each_clear_bit iterates sba_idx from 0 to SMC_LO_MAX_DMBS-1, and the check `if (sba_idx == SMC_LO_MAX_DMBS) return -ENOSPC;` ensures the index is always < SMC_LO_MAX_DMBS. In smcd_lo_alloc_dev (line 230): smcd->conn is allocated with `kcalloc(max_dmbs, sizeof(struct smc_connection *), GFP_KERNEL)` where max_dmbs = SMC_LO_MAX_DMBS. The hash lookup in smc_lo_move_data is protected by read_lock_bh(&ldev->dmb_ht_lock), preventing stale reads."}) | ok=True
